    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d458-a1">

                <pb facs="0762" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg666"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Server Pacha to Mr.
                            Brown</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte, Ministry of Foreign
                            Affairs</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1871-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 8,
                        1871</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received the note which you were so
                    good as to write to me the 25th October, containing the expression of the
                    regrets of the President of the United States on the occasion of the regrettable
                    death of His Highness Aali Pacha.</p>
                <p>The Sublime Porte has been very sensibly affected by the both noble and sincere
                    sentiments expressed by the President.</p>
                <p>I beg you, sir, to convey our very lively thanks to the President, and to assure
                    him that the new cabinet of His Imperial Majesty the Sultan can have nothing
                    more at heart than to cultivate more and more the relations of friendship so
                    happily existing between the two countries.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, the assurance of my perfect consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>SERVER.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
